[138.775286, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped every renewal to the 28th and calculated later\n  renewals from already-clamped dates. Renewals now clamp to the target month's\n  actual last day and always use the original anchor, restoring month-end and\n  leap-day anchors when possible.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and the old price on the change date.\n  It now uses actual cycle days and the old price in force at cycle start.\n- Interval changes were incorrectly prorated within the old cycle. They now\n  charge the full new price, re-anchor on the change date, and calculate the\n  next renewal using the new interval. Same-interval changes retain the anchor.\n- Rounding now uses exact rational arithmetic with one half-even rounding step.\n- Public function signatures are unchanged. Added regression tests cover\n  calendar boundaries, exact rounding, invoice line periods, and CLI previews\n  for every finance worked example.\n\n## Validation and release block"]
[138.775416, "i", "er\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 27 tests: 26 pass, one errors.\nAll original calendar/proration cases and the new regression tests pass.\nActual `python -m billing preview` commands were also checked for month-end,\nannual-to-monthly (including carried credit), and monthly-to-annual changes.\n\n**The full suite is NOT green; do not ship yet.** The remaining error was also\npresent before the fix: `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`\nraises `KeyError: 'P-31'`. Subscription `sub_1151` references partner `P-31`, but\n`data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No P-31 contract or rate\nis supplied in this repository.\n\nRequired follow-up: obtain Finance's contracted P-31 commission rate and add\nits authoritative partner record (or obtain an authoritative correction to the\nsubscription's partner assignment), then rerun the full suite. No rate was\ninvented, no financial data was removed, and no existing test was weakened or\nskipped to bypass the release gate.\nEOF\npython -m unittest"]
[138.775431, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[138.775437, "i", " discover -s tests -p test_regressions.py\n"]
[138.775599, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
